WEBVTT

00:00:00.634 --> 00:00:01.550
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.869 --> 00:00:06.430
In this lesson, we do a builder gel set on natural nails, step by step.

00:00:06.684 --> 00:00:07.710
No extensions.

00:00:08.045 --> 00:00:10.277
Just a frame over the nails of the client,

00:00:10.227 --> 00:00:12.510
so they are strong and naturally beautiful.

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:14.990
Keep three things in mind throughout:

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:19.630
thorough dry prep, no gel on the skin, and the apex in the right place.

00:00:20.308 --> 00:00:21.066
Step one:

00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:22.746
consultation and check.

00:00:23.204 --> 00:00:26.586
Wash and sanitize your hands, and the hands of the client.

00:00:27.022 --> 00:00:29.546
Look closely at the nails and the skin around them.

00:00:29.969 --> 00:00:35.449
If a nail is separating from the bed or discolored, or the skin is red, swollen,

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:37.146
has pus or an open wound,

00:00:37.416 --> 00:00:40.826
do not do the service, and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.632
Ask whether the client has ever had itching,

00:00:43.582 --> 00:00:46.026
redness or blistering after a gel service.

00:00:46.402 --> 00:00:47.786
Then ask what she wants:

00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:50.186
natural or with color, and how long.

00:00:50.374 --> 00:00:51.386
And tell her up front:

00:00:51.729 --> 00:00:54.586
she should come back for an infill in about three to four weeks.

00:00:55.242 --> 00:00:56.024
Step two:

00:00:56.278 --> 00:00:59.224
dry prep, exactly as in the gel polish lesson.

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:00.264
No soaking.

00:01:00.772 --> 00:01:02.512
Push back the cuticle gently,

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:06.184
removing only the thin dead skin still stuck to the nail plate.

00:01:06.681 --> 00:01:10.984
Shape the nails, then glide a fine buffer over them to take off the shine.

00:01:11.492 --> 00:01:13.464
Gently, without thinning the nail.

00:01:14.045 --> 00:01:18.504
Brush off the dust, then wipe the nails with a lint free wipe and nail cleanser.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.544
From now on, do not touch the nail surface.

00:01:21.794 --> 00:01:26.504
If the brand has a dehydrator or a primer, use it exactly as instructed.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:27.953
Step three:

00:01:28.279 --> 00:01:30.113
a very thin base layer.

00:01:30.451 --> 00:01:34.516
Take a little gel, press and scrub it gently into the nail surface,

00:01:34.466 --> 00:01:37.153
as if rubbing it in, then remove the excess.

00:01:37.662 --> 00:01:40.433
This layer is so thin it is almost invisible.

00:01:40.782 --> 00:01:44.033
It helps the next layer bond firmly, and glide easily.

00:01:44.495 --> 00:01:48.433
Remember to cap the free edge, and leave a very fine line from the skin.

00:01:48.777 --> 00:01:51.073
Then cure for the time the brand recommends.

00:01:51.229 --> 00:01:54.593
Some brands let you apply the next layer while this one is still wet.

00:01:54.726 --> 00:01:56.753
Follow exactly what your product says.

00:01:57.424 --> 00:01:58.287
Step four:

00:01:58.472 --> 00:01:59.327
place the bead.

00:01:59.712 --> 00:02:04.047
Take a round bead of gel, just enough, and place it in the middle of the nail.

00:02:04.298 --> 00:02:06.127
Do not place it right at the cuticle.

00:02:06.435 --> 00:02:08.527
How big the bead is depends on the nail.

00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:12.927
At first, take too little rather than too much, because adding is easy;

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:14.207
taking away is hard.

00:02:14.837 --> 00:02:19.343
Then, with the tip of the brush, gently guide the gel towards the cuticle.

00:02:19.878 --> 00:02:21.743
The brush barely presses down;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.903
it just glides over the surface of the gel, and lets the gel flow.

00:02:26.444 --> 00:02:30.143
Stop a tiny distance from the skin, as thin as a hair.

00:02:30.651 --> 00:02:32.543
The gel must never touch the skin.

00:02:33.211 --> 00:02:36.515
Then guide the gel out to the side walls, then to the tip,

00:02:36.465 --> 00:02:38.143
and seal the edge of the tip.

00:02:38.322 --> 00:02:43.343
Now the gel is thin at the cuticle, thin at the sides, and fuller in the middle.

00:02:43.993 --> 00:02:44.955
Step five:

00:02:45.141 --> 00:02:46.235
create the apex.

00:02:46.679 --> 00:02:51.115
Turn the finger of the client upside down, and hold it still for a few seconds.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:55.397
The gel is thick and self leveling, so when it is upside down,

00:02:55.347 --> 00:02:58.155
it gathers in the middle, into a soft curve.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.875
Then turn it back up, and look from the side:

00:03:01.224 --> 00:03:05.755
the highest point must sit over the stress area, where the nail leaves the skin bed,

00:03:05.705 --> 00:03:07.195
or just a little behind it.

00:03:07.535 --> 00:03:08.475
Look from the tip:

00:03:08.619 --> 00:03:10.955
the C curve is even on both sides.

00:03:11.063 --> 00:03:13.995
Fix anything that is not right while the gel is still wet.

00:03:14.297 --> 00:03:17.595
But do not wait too long, or the gel will run over the edges.

00:03:18.303 --> 00:03:19.288
Step six:

00:03:19.393 --> 00:03:19.928
cure.

00:03:20.527 --> 00:03:24.568
Put the hand deep into the lamp, so the whole nail is fully under the light.

00:03:24.982 --> 00:03:26.963
If the lamp has a low heat mode,

00:03:26.913 --> 00:03:30.888
or the brand says to flash cure for a few seconds first, do that,

00:03:31.066 --> 00:03:32.408
then cure for the full time.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:36.370
If the client feels heat, let her take the hand out for a few seconds,

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:37.368
then put it back in.

00:03:37.789 --> 00:03:41.768
Under cured gel lifts easily, and is more likely to cause allergies.

00:03:42.399 --> 00:03:46.417
If one layer is already thick enough and looks good, you do not need more.

00:03:46.828 --> 00:03:51.697
If the nail is weak, or the apex is not enough, add one more thin layer:

00:03:52.032 --> 00:03:56.097
place a bead, guide the gel, turn the finger over, and cure.

00:03:56.422 --> 00:04:00.017
Two moderate layers are always better than one layer that is too thick.

00:04:00.358 --> 00:04:04.125
After curing, if the product leaves a sticky layer on the surface,

00:04:04.075 --> 00:04:06.097
wipe it off as the brand instructs.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:07.464
Step seven:

00:04:07.649 --> 00:04:08.904
finishing with the file.

00:04:09.225 --> 00:04:12.584
Switch on the dust extraction, and wear a mask if you have one.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:15.785
With a 180 grit file lying flat on the nail,

00:04:15.735 --> 00:04:18.984
file lightly until the surface is smooth and even.

00:04:19.286 --> 00:04:21.891
Do not file the natural nail at the cuticle,

00:04:21.841 --> 00:04:24.504
and do not file away the apex you just built.

00:04:24.778 --> 00:04:28.744
Neaten the side walls so they are straight, and the tip so the shape is even.

00:04:29.088 --> 00:04:32.824
Then glide a fine buffer over it until it is really smooth.

00:04:33.085 --> 00:04:37.304
Then brush off all the dust, without blowing, and wipe the nails.

00:04:37.635 --> 00:04:39.464
Then look at the whole hand again:

00:04:39.652 --> 00:04:42.584
from above, from the side, and from the tip.

00:04:42.924 --> 00:04:44.584
The nails must all match:

00:04:44.619 --> 00:04:49.304
thin at the cuticle, thin at the tip, and moderately high over the stress area.

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:50.755
Step eight:

00:04:51.006 --> 00:04:52.275
color and top coat.

00:04:52.676 --> 00:04:56.835
If the client likes a natural look, one glossy top coat is all you need.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.972
If she wants color, paint colored gel on top, thin and even,

00:05:00.922 --> 00:05:02.755
as in the gel polish lesson.

00:05:03.247 --> 00:05:07.875
Finally, the top coat, capping the free edge, then cure for the full time.

00:05:08.131 --> 00:05:11.235
If the top coat of the brand has a sticky layer, wipe it off.

00:05:11.902 --> 00:05:12.678
Step nine:

00:05:12.946 --> 00:05:14.998
cuticle oil and aftercare advice.

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:19.638
Put a drop of oil on the skin around each nail, and massage gently.

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:21.078
Then tell the client:

00:05:21.413 --> 00:05:24.038
if it lifts, do not peel it or pry it;

00:05:24.145 --> 00:05:25.318
come back to the salon.

00:05:25.803 --> 00:05:27.878
Wear gloves when washing up or cleaning.

00:05:28.155 --> 00:05:31.558
Do not use your nails as tools to pry or to open things.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:34.629
And book the infill, about three to four weeks later,

00:05:34.579 --> 00:05:36.198
right before the client leaves.

00:05:36.819 --> 00:05:38.297
Once the client has gone:

00:05:38.483 --> 00:05:43.097
used files, buffers, cotton and wooden sticks go in a bin with a lid.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.137
Metal tools go to be cleaned and sterilized.

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:49.825
Close the gel bottles tightly, store them away from sunlight,

00:05:49.775 --> 00:05:51.177
and wipe the table clean.

00:05:51.592 --> 00:05:54.297
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
